(2) 
Interjurisdictional Intelligence System
 means an intelligence system which involves two or more participating agencies representing different governmental units or jurisdictions;

(4) 
Participating Agency
 means an agency of local, county, State, Federal, or other governmental unit which exercises law enforcement or criminal investigation authority and which is authorized to submit and receive criminal intelligence information through an interjurisdictional intelligence system. A participating agency may be a member or a nonmember of an interjurisdictional intelligence system;
